# Security overrides for vulnerable *build-time* tooling.
#
# Scope: transitive dependencies of the build itself (Gradle plugins, annotation
# processors, code generators). Runtime/shipped dependencies belong in
# `gradle/libs.versions.toml`, not here.
#
# Why this file exists separately: a forced version constraint applied to fix a
# CVE is a security decision with a different review bar and a different lifetime
# than an ordinary dependency bump. Keeping the two apart means a reviewer can
# see at a glance what is pinned *for security* and why, and stale pins can be
# retired once the upstream fix lands naturally.
#
# Format: one `group:artifact=version` per line, '#' comments.
# Every entry MUST carry an advisory reference and the reason it is still needed.
#
# Example (illustrative only -- not an active override):
#   # GHSA-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx -- arbitrary file write during archive extraction.
#   # Remove once the plugin that pulls this in ships a fixed release.
#   org.apache.commons:commons-compress=1.28.0

# No build-tool security overrides are active.
#
# This is expected: the repository does not yet contain a Gradle build, so there
# is no build-tool dependency graph to constrain. Entries will be added here if
# and only if a CVE affecting build tooling cannot be resolved by an ordinary
# version bump in `gradle/libs.versions.toml`.
